* The Prize Shop\n(betting stickers)
** The question
*** A judge promises to\nannounce the answer
*** One box per possible\nanswer
*** The judge can only\nanswer once
** Swapping money\nfor stickers
*** Put in 1 coin,\nget one sticker\nfor every answer
*** The full set is\nalways worth 1 coin
*** Hand the full set back,\nget your coin back
** Cashing in
*** Wait for the judge
*** Winning sticker\nbecomes a coin
*** Losing stickers\nbecome nothing
** Two questions at once
*** "Alice wins AND\nit rains"
*** Build it race-first\nor rain-first
*** Both routes must land\non the SAME sticker
** Naming the stickers
*** Every sticker needs\na serial number
*** Rule 1: order must\nnot change the name
*** Rule 2: nobody can\ninvent a fake name
** The bad first idea
*** Turn each label into\na big number, then add
*** Order did not matter\n(good)
*** But a cheater can hunt\nfor numbers that add up\nto a name they want
** The fix\n(spots on a curve)
*** Each label becomes\na spot on a curved line
*** Spots add together to\nmake another spot
*** Order still does\nnot matter
*** Working backwards is\na puzzle nobody\nhas solved
** The counter mistake
*** Clerk handed out new\nstickers before taking\nthe old one
*** Sneaky customer used\nthat gap to cash in twice
*** Fix: take first,\nhand over after
** Why it matters
*** The money box always\nholds enough for\nevery sticker
*** Real websites use this\nto run prediction markets
@endmindmap
